WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.640
Speaker 1: So I want to start today with what's&nbsp;
really fundamentally an infrastructure story, but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:11.360
also a story about how we often sort of miss the&nbsp;
forest for the trees or we end up wrapped up in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.360 --> 00:00:16.320
a detail when the bigger story is really the big&nbsp;
picture. Many of you might have heard about this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:21.280
bridge collapse that took place in Pittsburgh,&nbsp;
and because of the timing of a Joe Biden&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:26.240
trip to Pennsylvania, it immediately became very,&nbsp;
very political. We're even going to look at a clip&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.240 --> 00:00:32.880
on Fox News of a couple of anchors there talking&nbsp;
about the collapse and Joe Biden's infrastructure&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:37.600
bill and just getting at just about every&nbsp;
single fact wrong. But before we get to that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:43.600
I think it's important to remind you guys that&nbsp;
when we talk about infrastructure and the fact&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:49.200
that the U.S. is woefully behind on infrastructure&nbsp;
spending, that infrastructure spending,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:57.040
which in many countries is not political in the&nbsp;
U.S., is so politicized and Partizan that we have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.600 --> 00:01:05.520
hundreds of bridges with the exact same rating as&nbsp;
the Pittsburgh Bridge that collapsed. And yet we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.520 --> 00:01:11.520
only talk about the issue in real serious terms&nbsp;
when a bridge actually collapses, when we have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.520 --> 00:01:18.000
debates about infrastructure. It is mentioned in&nbsp;
passing, Hey, we have many bridges that need to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:25.360
repaired, brought back, modernized, et cetera.&nbsp;
But it's almost like it doesn't really exist&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.360 --> 00:01:29.120
until there's a bridge collapse. And case&nbsp;
in point, there's a very good article on New&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.120 --> 00:01:37.120
Jersey dot com NJ.com, which points out nearly 500&nbsp;
New Jersey bridges received the same poor rating&nbsp;&nbsp;

