Garden State Bridges received a grade of&nbsp;
poor. That's the same rating as the bridge&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.360 --> 00:02:06.960
in Pittsburgh's Frick Park that collapsed on&nbsp;
Friday morning, injuring 10 people. States,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:13.040
federal agencies and tribal governments submit&nbsp;
data to the bridge inventory on an annual basis.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.040 --> 00:02:19.520
About seven percent of Jersey Bridges&nbsp;
have that poor grade, 27 percent are good,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.520 --> 00:02:22.880
which is the highest rating, and&nbsp;
the rest are somewhere in between.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.840 --> 00:02:28.080
Each bridge receives ratings on its deck,&nbsp;
superstructure substructure and culvert,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:34.320
et cetera, et cetera. So also&nbsp;
important is that many of these are&nbsp;&nbsp;

